+## One-page quick-start (copy-paste) 🚀
+Prereqs: Java 17+, Maven, Node 18+, Docker (optional).
+
+1. Frontend (dev):
+   cd "SuperMarket New Frontend" && npm install && npm run dev
+2. Backend (local profile):
+   cd "SuperMarket Backend" && ./mvnw.cmd -DskipTests package && java -jar target/SuperMarketBackend-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar --spring.profiles.active=local
+3. Start both (helper): `start-dev.ps1`
+4. E2E (Playwright): cd "SuperMarket New Frontend" && npx playwright install && npm run test:e2e
+5. Docker (prod-like): from repo root `cp .env.example .env` and `docker-compose up -d --build`
+
+## Checklist — Adding a new API / endpoint 🧭
+- Add controller under `SuperMarket Backend/src/main/java/in/main/controller/` with `@RequestMapping("/api/your")` and HTTP methods.
+- Implement business logic in a new or existing `service/` class.
+- Add DB access in `repository/` (extend `JpaRepository`) and update `entities/` if schema changes are required.
+- Add DTOs and mappers if the payload differs from entities.
+- Protect the endpoint via roles in `JwtSecurityConfig` (if admin-only use `/api/admin/**`).
+- Add unit tests (service) and integration/E2E tests for cross-stack flows. Use `/api/dev/**` helpers for test data when available.
+- Update `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md` and `.env.example` if new services or env vars are required.
+
